  "steps": [
    "Heat the olive oil in a large soup pot over a medium heat. Add the onion, carrots and celery with a pinch of the measured salt, then cook for 8 minutes, stirring often, until softened but not browned.",
    "Add the garlic and cook for 1 minute until fragrant. Stir in the courgette and potato, then cook for 3 minutes to coat the vegetables in the oil.",
    "Add the tomato paste, dried oregano, dried thyme and bay leaf. Stir for 1 minute until the tomato paste darkens slightly.",
    "Pour in the canned tomatoes and vegetable stock. Add the remaining salt and the black pepper, bring to a boil, then reduce to a steady simmer. Cook for 15 minutes, until the potato is just tender.",
    "Stir in the cannellini beans and pasta. Simmer for 10 to 12 minutes, stirring occasionally, until the pasta is al dente and the soup has thickened slightly.",
    "Add the chopped kale and simmer for 3 to 4 minutes, until wilted and tender. Remove the bay leaf.",
    "Taste and adjust seasoning if needed. Ladle into bowls and finish with chopped parsley."
  ],
